      "side": 1,
      "message": "Without this change, when a LEA disconnected, handleGroupTransitToInactive is called twice anyway.\n\nFirst: \nhttps://source.corp.google.com/android/packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/le_audio/LeAudioService.java;l\u003d964?q\u003dleaudioservice.java\u0026sq\u003dpackage:%5Eandroid$%7C%5Eaosp-androidx$\n\nSecond:\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/android/packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/le_audio/LeAudioService.java;l\u003d1333?q\u003dleaudioservice.java\u0026sq\u003dpackage:%5Eandroid$%7C%5Eaosp-androidx$\n\n\nAnd I just realized that I miss read Telecom and/or Bluetooth code.\nI made this change because I saw a log from Telecom that says \n\"BluetoothRouteManager: More than one profile reporting active devices.\"\nand I found the inactivate wasn\u0027t notified.\nHowever, the LeAudioService.getActiveDevices always returns two devices. So, now I don\u0027t know why it is fixed with this CL :(",
